ew of us in the office have had the  experience on playstation 4 where the  main menu spins up our console's fans to  an alarming speed we've even had our  console shut down from overheating  because of the main menu  at this stage we'd probably settle for a  simple text based menu that doesn't make  your ps4 scream in agony over the screen  where your character  walks infinitely towards something  fortnite never did us like that  number five run faster fist out we've  had it good with movement in apex for  far too long to go back when that gas  cloud is closing in and you're carrying  heavy weapons that reduce your run speed  to john woo levels of  you really need to be able to put your  weapons away and run faster  like significantly faster it's true that  there are ways to build this with double  time and a knife but we want it  all the time number six events it may  just not have happened yet but we were  hoping season four would have character  drama and huge map  changes nukes going off and unique  challenges so far we've  opened a few bunkers been stuck on a  frozen winter map through the summer  sold a bunch of cold winter themed items  we get it  someone loves winter it's just that  fortnite has been doing amazing map  altering events  and you had to be there moments for  years now it's hard to get excited for  characters we know nothing about give us  the good stuff the animated shorts the  stories outside of the game  there are leaks that season 5 might  finally deliver on some of this  and we're ready number 7 armor the  number of folks here at gamespot would  like to see the game's armor system  change  the current armor causes players to  waste plates because it's limited to  filling or topping off one of three bars  instead it should give you a fixed  number of armor points the full  50 per plate preferably and potentially  spill over from one armor bar  into the next we could also use a bit  more variety in terms of  armor types and rarity number eight  teachable challenges  one of the best games of all time  titanfall it's just facts  had a system of challenges that forced  you to get good with each weapon  those challenges were based on showing  the player what a gun was made to do  far too many challenges in warzone are  simply chores or have nothing to do with  the weapon blueprint that they unlock  we're talking even simple stuff like  teaching players to make sniper kills  from the edge of the gas  or experiment with different rockets for  different situations while we're here  some of the challenges are still just  broken  and that can be frustrating overall the  rewards for warzone challenges just  aren't very good and that needs to  change number nine  improved climbing system far too many  times you'll be on the run from the gas  and get hung up on cliffsides or rocks  when it comes to terrain there isn't a  good way to tell  what is and isn't climbable and there's  nothing worse than getting got  because your ankle snagged it'd be nice  if players could reliably understand  what can and can't be scaled in the heat  of battle number 10  golf masks equipping the gas mask should  be a one time thing  the automatic animation that plays while  taking the mask off near the edge of the  gas  messes with gun play and gets players  killed number 11  balance man this is a tricky one to give  credit where it's due there have been  plenty of balance changes like nerfing  the growl  and making loadout drops more expensive  it's just that there isn't a lot of room  for creativity with perks in the final  circles if you don't have cold blooded  to stay off thermal sniper scopes or eod  so you don't get vaporized by c4  and rpgs you're at a huge disadvantage  we'd like to see fewer dominant tactics  and more risk reward when it comes to  loadout creativity  in general keep up the good work  infinity ward so what are your ideas on  balance and how to improve warzone what  just sticks in your cry when you play  let us